==English==
{{wikipedia|Jumping the shark}}

===Etymology===
From a moment on the TV series ''[[w:Happy Days|Happy Days]]'' in which the character Fonzie jumped over a shark on waterskis.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=[[jump]] [[the]] [[shark]]|jumps the shark|jumped the shark|jumping the shark}}

# {{idiom|of a [[television program]] or other [[narrative]]}} To undergo a [[storyline]] development which is so [[ridiculous]] that previous [[quality]] is considered to have been lost.
#: ''Happy Days '''jumped the shark''' when Fonzie jumped over a shark on waterskis.''
#* '''2007''', [[w:Jeph Jacques|Jeph Jacques]], ''[http://questionablecontent.net/view.php?comic=951 Time To Add A Cute Kid To The Cast]'' Questionable Content Number 951
#*: Pintsize: Wait, don’t you want to know why I’m tied up and hanging from the ceiling?
#*: Faye: Not really.  Nighty night!
#*: Pintsize: Shit! My wacky antics have '''jumped the shark'''!

